hacker mode is battlefield hardlines  replacement for the previous games  commander mode given hardlines cops  versus criminals focus you're not going  to be dropping cruise missiles on  people's heads as the hacker instead  you'll be taking over cameras and  providing intelligence to your teammates  while disrupting the enemy by setting  off gas systems and jamming their GPS  signals you can view the action from a  map perspective a top-down perspective  or by looking over the shoulder of any  squad leader plus you've got some cool  abilities let's take a look at each one  and explain how best to use them hacking  lets you take control of objects in the  map like cameras gas systems and power  transformers hacking a camera will cause  it to automatically spot enemies in its  view distance for the rest of your team  revealing them on everyone's mini-map  you can also look through the camera  yourself to get a better angle of  interior locations something your  traditional top-down view wouldn't  usually allow take over as many cameras  as you can as early as possible and your  team will have eyes on most of the map  before you've even cracked the vault gas  systems and transformers can be hacked  so that they automatically explode when  an enemy is near stunning and  disorienting them they'll need to  recharge for a short time after  exploding so only hack these when you're  ready to coordinate movements with the  rest of your team  GPS spotting is like a UAV that reveals  enemy positions in a small area on the  map for a short amount of time  use this as often as possible in areas  where your hacked cameras can't already  see GPS jamming acts as a kind of  counter for GPS spotting hiding your  teammates position in an area and  preventing them from being spotted if  you don't want the enemy to know which  way your team is breaking into a vault  from in heist mode drop a jamming signal  over their point of entry the  traceability scans the entire  battlefield to show high-value targets  like enemies spawn beacons and squad  leaders on the map you can then give  orders to your own squad leaders to  attack these targets it's also a great  way to point out the locations of pesky  snipers at the edge of a map one ability  the hacker can use on their own  teammates is the squad upgrade this  increases the rate at which that squad  receives reputation perks  basically reward like extra armor or  grenades that only exists for that match  use this like a carrot for squads that  are being good and following your orders  fast deploy is another ability you can  use on one of your own squads it reduces  the time it takes for members of that  squad to reform this is really useful  for squads who are leading the charge in  heist mode and are expecting to take a  lot of casualties very quickly  finally overclock is an ability to have  replies to themselves to reduce the  cooldown time of their other abilities  the catch is some abilities may overheat  making them unavailable for a short time  it's a randomized risk but if you're  waiting for everything to cool down  there's no harm in using it with these  abilities battlefield hardlines hacker  mode plays like a smaller scale tighter  and more focused version of the prior  command emotes its most useful in  hardline heist mode where situational  awareness is crucial and least useful in  Hotwire mode where everyone's too busy  getting in car chases or flipping  choppers you're rarely going to get to a  top of a leaderboard playing a full  match as the hacker so just do it as a  favor for your team besides you can  switch back to a regular infantry role  mid game but the reward in seeing your  fellow criminals get away with bags cash  as the pursuing cops are caught in a  cloud of gas it's worth it  you
 

